	<body>
		<segment id="1" parent="192" relname="joint-list">SJC 13660 .</segment>
		<segment id="2" parent="192" relname="joint-list">Commonwealth versus Elena Gaston .</segment>
		<segment id="3" parent="4" relname="organization-phatic">Okay , Attorney .</segment>
		<segment id="4" parent="170" relname="span">Whenever you 're ready .</segment>
		<segment id="5" parent="241" relname="span">Good afternoon .</segment>
		<segment id="6" parent="193" relname="span">May it please the court .</segment>
		<segment id="7" parent="242" relname="joint-list">My name is Andrew ,</segment>
		<segment id="8" parent="242" relname="joint-list">and I represent Elena Gaston .</segment>
		<segment id="9" parent="169" relname="span">This case presents an issue</segment>
		<segment id="10" parent="9" relname="elaboration-attribute">that this court has never confronted ,</segment>
		<segment id="11" parent="246" relname="span">and that is whether a potential future claim of ineffective assistance can create a manifest necessity for a mistrial .</segment>
		<segment id="12" parent="13" relname="attribution-negative">But I do n't think</segment>
		<segment id="13" parent="244" relname="span">this court actually needs to reach that broader question ,</segment>
		<segment id="14" parent="168" relname="span">because the question</segment>
		<segment id="15" parent="14" relname="elaboration-attribute">presented on these facts</segment>
		<segment id="16" parent="249" relname="same-unit">is actually much narrower ,</segment>
		<segment id="17" parent="167" relname="span">and that is whether there was a manifest necessity</segment>
		<segment id="18" parent="166" relname="span">where one , the judge erroneously inferred a complete lack of consultation</segment>
		<segment id="19" parent="18" relname="causal-cause">based on counsel 's statements about the opening .</segment>
		<segment id="20" parent="21" relname="attribution-positive">Two , where the judge appears to have mistakenly believed</segment>
		<segment id="21" parent="171" relname="span">that the defendant 's explicit consent is required prior to a concession .</segment>
		<segment id="22" parent="251" relname="joint-list">And three , the defendant neither alleged a lack of consultation --</segment>
		<segment id="23" parent="252" relname="organization-phatic">So sorry ,</segment>
		<segment id="24" parent="252" relname="joint-list">Defense Attorney argues jury nullification</segment>
		<segment id="25" parent="252" relname="joint-list">and examines on jury nullification .</segment>
		<segment id="26" parent="254" relname="span">What 's the judge to do ?</segment>
		<segment id="27" parent="26" relname="adversative-antithesis">Just let it go forward ?</segment>
		<segment id="28" parent="29" relname="attribution-positive">Well , in terms of the jury nullification issue , I believe</segment>
		<segment id="29" parent="256" relname="span">the judge addressed that .</segment>
		<segment id="30" parent="260" relname="span">That was sort of the first potential basis for the mistrial</segment>
		<segment id="31" parent="30" relname="elaboration-attribute">that he considered .</segment>
		<segment id="32" parent="257" relname="joint-sequence">Um , he gave a forceful curative instruction ,</segment>
		<segment id="33" parent="34" relname="attribution-positive">and he found repeatedly and explicitly</segment>
		<segment id="34" parent="178" relname="span">that the jury could and would follow it</segment>
		<segment id="35" parent="178" relname="causal-result">so there could be no prejudice to the Commonwealth .</segment>
		<segment id="36" parent="313" relname="span">And then the defense attorney just does it again ,</segment>
		<segment id="37" parent="36" relname="organization-phatic">right ?</segment>
		<segment id="38" parent="267" relname="span">Well , no .</segment>
		<segment id="39" parent="264" relname="attribution-positive">I think</segment>
		<segment id="40" parent="263" relname="context-circumstance">if you when you look closely at the record ,</segment>
		<segment id="41" parent="42" relname="attribution-positive">you 'll see</segment>
		<segment id="42" parent="263" relname="span">that even prior to , um , the , the evidentiary portion of the trial beginning , there 's some motions in limine about what kind of questions can be asked .</segment>
		<segment id="43" parent="179" relname="attribution-positive">And he says</segment>
		<segment id="44" parent="45" relname="adversative-concession">" even though force and coercion are not elements ,</segment>
		<segment id="45" parent="179" relname="span">you are allowed to inquire about that " .</segment>
		<segment id="46" parent="237" relname="attribution-positive">And the judge says</segment>
		<segment id="47" parent="237" relname="span">there was n't anything surprising about the cross-examination .</segment>
		<segment id="48" parent="47" relname="explanation-evidence">" I expected there to be questions about lack of force , lack of coercion . "</segment>
		<segment id="49" parent="271" relname="attribution-positive">Um , so I think</segment>
		<segment id="50" parent="271" relname="same-unit">that</segment>
		<segment id="51" parent="270" relname="joint-list">where the judge has given that forceful instruction</segment>
		<segment id="52" parent="183" relname="attribution-positive">and where he has found repeatedly and explicitly ,</segment>
		<segment id="53" parent="183" relname="joint-list">the jury can</segment>
		<segment id="54" parent="183" relname="joint-list">and will abide by it ,</segment>
		<segment id="55" parent="184" relname="span">that sort of closes the book .</segment>
		<segment id="56" parent="273" relname="span">But it 's sort of a combination ,</segment>
		<segment id="57" parent="56" relname="restatement-partial">is n't it ?</segment>
		<segment id="58" parent="59" relname="organization-phatic">Because it 's</segment>
		<segment id="59" parent="272" relname="span">it 's not just that the opening argued jury nullification .</segment>
		<segment id="60" parent="187" relname="span">It 's that the opening foreclosed the only defense</segment>
		<segment id="61" parent="60" relname="elaboration-attribute">that had been articulated by defense counsel to the judge ,</segment>
		<segment id="62" parent="187" relname="elaboration-attribute">which is lack of knowledge .</segment>
		<segment id="63" parent="191" relname="organization-preparation">So the the the opening did two things .</segment>
		<segment id="64" parent="65" relname="organization-phatic">It both removed --</segment>
		<segment id="65" parent="277" relname="span">It basically undermined that defense , the only defense</segment>
		<segment id="66" parent="191" relname="joint-sequence">and then also argued jury nullification .</segment>
		<segment id="67" parent="279" relname="same-unit">So do n't we need to look at that in ,</segment>
		<segment id="68" parent="69" relname="organization-phatic">you know ,</segment>
		<segment id="69" parent="195" relname="span">both of those together</segment>
		<segment id="70" parent="194" relname="span">when we 're reviewing , um , the judge 's decision</segment>
		<segment id="71" parent="280" relname="restatement-repetition">to allow the mistrial</segment>
		<segment id="72" parent="280" relname="restatement-repetition">or grant the mistrial ?</segment>
		<segment id="73" parent="199" relname="span">I disagree</segment>
		<segment id="74" parent="197" relname="span">because you have the trial judge making that factual finding</segment>
		<segment id="75" parent="190" relname="joint-list">that the jury can</segment>
		<segment id="76" parent="190" relname="joint-list">and would follow the curative instruction .</segment>
		<segment id="77" parent="198" relname="span">And under Arizona v Washington , we defer to that trial judge 's assessment</segment>
		<segment id="78" parent="77" relname="explanation-justify">because the trial judge observed the jurors during their voir dire .</segment>
		<segment id="79" parent="201" relname="span">They -- he observed the opening</segment>
		<segment id="80" parent="79" relname="context-circumstance">as it was given .</segment>
		<segment id="81" parent="200" relname="joint-list">He observed the tone .</segment>
		<segment id="82" parent="200" relname="joint-list">He observed the jurors during the curative instruction .</segment>
		<segment id="83" parent="203" relname="span">And for those reasons , we have to defer a finding .</segment>
		<segment id="84" parent="206" relname="restatement-repetition">Was there a finding ?</segment>
		<segment id="85" parent="205" relname="span">Was there a finding</segment>
		<segment id="86" parent="87" relname="attribution-positive">that the judge believed</segment>
		<segment id="87" parent="204" relname="span">that the instruction would be followed ,</segment>
		<segment id="88" parent="282" relname="joint-disjunction">or was it ?</segment>
		<segment id="89" parent="284" relname="span">Yes .</segment>
		<segment id="90" parent="89" relname="evaluation-comment">Okay .</segment>
		<segment id="91" parent="283" relname="restatement-repetition">Yes he does .</segment>
		<segment id="92" parent="211" relname="organization-phatic">Um , and I can --</segment>
		<segment id="93" parent="209" relname="attribution-positive">But I think</segment>
		<segment id="94" parent="208" relname="attribution-positive">the judge said</segment>
		<segment id="95" parent="208" relname="span">that that was based on his assessment at the time</segment>
		<segment id="96" parent="95" relname="elaboration-attribute">he made that ruling .</segment>
		<segment id="97" parent="210" relname="span">And then after that , there were three witnesses</segment>
		<segment id="98" parent="97" relname="elaboration-attribute">called</segment>
		<segment id="99" parent="286" relname="same-unit">and the subject matter of the cross-examination .</segment>
		<segment id="100" parent="314" relname="organization-phatic">I 'm sorry , um .</segment>
		<segment id="101" parent="212" relname="span">The subject matter of the cross-examination continued down the same line ,</segment>
		<segment id="102" parent="101" relname="elaboration-attribute">which was lack of compulsion ,</segment>
		<segment id="103" parent="212" relname="organization-phatic">right ?</segment>
		<segment id="104" parent="105" relname="organization-phatic">It did n't</segment>
		<segment id="105" parent="214" relname="span">it did n't try to do anything with the maybe a legally relevant -- a legally relevant line of defense .</segment>
		<segment id="106" parent="289" relname="organization-phatic">Well , again , I would say --</segment>
		<segment id="107" parent="289" relname="span">Well , just as an initial matter , so the judge adheres to his conclusion</segment>
		<segment id="108" parent="216" relname="joint-list">that the jury could</segment>
		<segment id="109" parent="216" relname="joint-list">and would follow it .</segment>
		<segment id="110" parent="218" relname="joint-sequence">So you want us to defer to the judge 's findings , the first finding ,</segment>
		<segment id="111" parent="291" relname="joint-list">and then ignore the judge 's finding later on</segment>
		<segment id="112" parent="113" relname="attribution-positive">and say</segment>
		<segment id="113" parent="217" relname="span">there 's an abuse of discretion ?</segment>
		<segment id="114" parent="220" relname="adversative-antithesis">No , I 'm not asking you to ignore the finding .</segment>
		<segment id="115" parent="220" relname="span">I 'm saying the finding</segment>
		<segment id="116" parent="219" relname="span">about whether the efficacy of the curative instruction is a particular type of finding</segment>
		<segment id="117" parent="116" relname="elaboration-attribute">that we defer to .</segment>
		<segment id="118" parent="297" relname="span">And the judge does say ,</segment>
		<segment id="119" parent="118" relname="explanation-evidence">it 's at page 185 --</segment>
		<segment id="120" parent="300" relname="span">But</segment>
		<segment id="121" parent="120" relname="mode-manner">unrepentant ,</segment>
		<segment id="122" parent="299" relname="same-unit">the lawyer just keeps doing the same thing witness after witness ,</segment>
		<segment id="123" parent="299" relname="restatement-partial">correct ?</segment>
		<segment id="124" parent="225" relname="span">No , I disagree ,</segment>
		<segment id="125" parent="301" relname="span">and the judge disagreed as well ,</segment>
		<segment id="126" parent="302" relname="same-unit">because</segment>
		<segment id="127" parent="128" relname="context-circumstance">when the Commonwealth makes that argument ,</segment>
		<segment id="128" parent="303" relname="span">the judge says ,</segment>
		<segment id="129" parent="222" relname="span">" actually , I was not surprised by anything</segment>
		<segment id="130" parent="129" relname="elaboration-attribute">that happened during cross-examination ;</segment>
		<segment id="131" parent="221" relname="span">we had this discussion prior to trial</segment>
		<segment id="132" parent="131" relname="elaboration-attribute">that he would be allowed to inquire into that " .</segment>
		<segment id="133" parent="134" relname="adversative-concession">It 's not an element ,</segment>
		<segment id="134" parent="304" relname="span">but it 's a proper basis for inquiry .</segment>
		<segment id="135" parent="228" relname="attribution-positive">Um , so I think</segment>
		<segment id="136" parent="228" relname="span">that the judge has addressed that situation</segment>
		<segment id="137" parent="136" relname="causal-result">and you have to defer to his finding on that ,</segment>
		<segment id="138" parent="310" relname="span">and he does continue to adhere to it on Monday , the day of the mistrial .</segment>
		<segment id="139" parent="306" relname="same-unit">So</segment>
		<segment id="140" parent="141" relname="explanation-justify">if you look at the transcripts , page 12 and 14 ,</segment>
		<segment id="141" parent="305" relname="span">he says</segment>
		<segment id="142" parent="143" relname="attribution-positive">" I continue to believe</segment>
		<segment id="143" parent="230" relname="span">the jury would follow this instruction " .</segment>
		<segment id="144" parent="233" relname="span">And it 's not until the Commonwealth raises this issue of lack of consultation</segment>
		<segment id="145" parent="144" relname="elaboration-attribute">that I am now reconsidering .</segment>
		<segment id="146" parent="147" relname="context-circumstance">I came into court today</segment>
		<segment id="147" parent="308" relname="span">ready to reaffirm my denial of the mistrial ,</segment>
		<segment id="148" parent="309" relname="joint-sequence">and then the Commonwealth raised this issue for the first time .</segment>
		<segment id="149" parent="150" relname="attribution-positive">And on the basis of that , I find</segment>
		<segment id="150" parent="234" relname="span">there 's manifest necessity .</segment>
		<segment id="151" parent="235" relname="span">The problem with that finding is that it 's predicated on this erroneous factual finding</segment>
		<segment id="152" parent="151" relname="elaboration-attribute">that there is a total lack of consultation ,</segment>
		<segment id="153" parent="235" relname="organization-phatic">right ?</segment>
		<segment id="154" parent="316" relname="span">What trial counsel says is I did n't talk to her about my opening specifically .</segment>
		<segment id="155" parent="319" relname="span">There 's no other information .</segment>
		<segment id="156" parent="173" relname="topic-question">The judge asks him once .</segment>
		<segment id="157" parent="158" relname="attribution-positive">He says</segment>
		<segment id="158" parent="173" relname="span">" no , I did n't speak to her about my opening " .</segment>
		<segment id="159" parent="175" relname="attribution-positive">The judge later says</segment>
		<segment id="160" parent="161" relname="attribution-positive">" well , did n't you just tell me</segment>
		<segment id="161" parent="175" relname="span">you did n't talk to her about your opening ? "</segment>
		<segment id="162" parent="163" relname="attribution-positive">And he says</segment>
		<segment id="163" parent="172" relname="span">" yes , that 's correct " .</segment>
		<segment id="164" parent="177" relname="span">Those are the only two questions</segment>
		<segment id="165" parent="164" relname="elaboration-attribute">we have .</segment>
		<group id="166" type="span" parent="251" relname="joint-list"/>
